[issue.1776]
number = 1776
title = "[Coherence] The existing 0x0907 ABI freeze test still expects four methods and one event, so it fails now that the ABI has bindPeer, peerBinding and PeerAttestationBound"
revision = "a910fdedd579e63379ae6c2e4d4971990d28f8ad"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "Commit 6e64aa6ffb45918b2936a2c2c92b248687a88287 added the peer-binding entries still served by precompiles/layerxagent/teeattestor/teeattestor.go:46, :47 and :48, making six methods and two events, but precompiles/layerxagent/teeattestor/teeattestor_test.go:329 and :366 still require four and one and its table at :334 omits both peer methods despite their gas schedules at precompiles/layerxagent/teeattestor/teeattestor.go:143; the issue's claim about the original verification command is incorrect because spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:296863 selects only TestPeerBinding, whose selector and event checks at precompiles/layerxagent/teeattestor/peer_binding_test.go:47 and :69 do not repair the freeze test."
close_comment = "The 0x0907 ABI freeze test still describes four methods and one event although peer binding expands the interface to six methods and two events. The follow-up task will freeze the complete interface, including peer-binding selectors, gas schedules, return types and event fields, while preserving existing coverage."

